## 10. Constraints

{{git_policy_summary}}

**Hard constraints:**
- NEVER `git commit` in the worktree. NEVER `git push` or `git pull`. The orchestrator commits and merges.
- ALWAYS `git add` (stage) before returning. The orchestrator reads `git status --porcelain` to verify staging.
- NEVER edit files outside `{{worktree_abs_path}}` (canonical) or `{{report_abs_path}}` (AI workspace report).
- NEVER invoke the Task tool (subagents cannot nest in v0.1).

**Return format on completion:**

```json
{
  "mode": "complete",
  "report_path": "{{report_abs_path}}",
  "summary": "<one-line summary, max ~120 chars>",
  "stage_status": "all_staged | partial | none"
}
```

